---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import policy from '../../../PRIVACY.md?raw';
import { marked } from 'marked';
// Keep the website disclosure tied to the app's canonical privacy document.
const html = await marked.parse(policy);
---
<Layout title="Privacy — Alba" description="How Alba handles your photos, account details and optional diagnostics."><article class="document"><p class="eyebrow">Your photos stay yours.</p><div set:html={html}></div><h2>Privacy questions</h2><p>Contact Luca at <a href="mailto:alba@lvca.me">alba@lvca.me</a> with questions about Alba’s handling of your data. You can remove Alba’s locally stored data through Android’s app settings.</p><h2 id="website">This website</h2><p>With your permission, this website uses Google Analytics to understand page visits, referral sources, and interactions such as outbound links. Analytics uses cookies to distinguish visits and sends usage and device information to Google. It loads only on alba.lvca.me after you select Accept. If you reject analytics, no Google Analytics script is loaded. You can change your choice or withdraw consent using Analytics preferences in the footer; withdrawing consent removes this site’s Analytics cookies.</p><p>Analytics cookies expire after up to six months unless renewed by another visit. Advertising personalization and Google signals are disabled. Learn <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google processes data from sites using its services</a>. This website analytics setup does not add tracking to the Alba Android app.</p><p>The site stores your analytics choice and your chosen light or dark appearance locally in your browser. The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub logs visitors’ IP addresses for security purposes, as described in its <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">privacy statement</a>.</p></article></Layout>
